echo "Route ID: $ROUTE_ID"

=========



Step 15.4 – Enable automatic deployment
Purpose: We will create the $default stage with automatic deployment enabled. This ensures API Gateway publishes the route and integration without requiring a separate deployment command after every configuration change.

Run:
aws apigatewayv2 create-stage \
  --api-id "$API_ID" \
  --stage-name '$default' \
  --auto-deploy \
  --region "$AWS_REGION"


Now capture the API endpoint:
export API_ENDPOINT=$(aws apigatewayv2 get-api \
  --api-id "$API_ID" \
  --region "$AWS_REGION" \
  --query 'ApiEndpoint' \
  --output text)

echo "Chatbot API endpoint: ${API_ENDPOINT}/chat"


===========

Step 15.5 – Allow API Gateway to invoke Lambda
Purpose: Creating the integration does not automatically grant API Gateway permission to invoke Lambda. We must add a resource-based permission to the Lambda function.

Run:
aws lambda add-permission \
  --function-name day2-rag-chat \
  --statement-id AllowAPIGatewayInvoke \
  --action lambda:InvokeFunction \
  --principal apigateway.amazonaws.com \
  --source-arn "arn:aws:execute-api:${AWS_REGION}:${ACCOUNT_ID}:${API_ID}/*/*/chat" \
  --region "$AWS_REGION"

==========

Step 16.1 – Prepare the chatbot frontend
Purpose: We will create a browser-based chat interface using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. It will send questions to the API Gateway endpoint and display the answers returned by Bedrock.

We will keep the frontend simple and dependency-free, using vanilla JavaScript.

In your existing frontend directory, run:


cat > index.html <<'EOF'
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Day 2 | Bedrock RAG Assistant</title>

  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background: #f3f5f9;
      color: #202b3c;
    }

    header {
      background: #172b4d;
      color: white;
      padding: 22px 30px;
    }

    header h1 {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    header p {
      margin: 7px 0 0;
      color: #cbd5e1;
    }

    .container {
      max-width: 900px;
      margin: 30px auto;
      padding: 0 16px;
    }

    .chat-box {
      background: white;
      border-radius: 14px;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 20px #00000010;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    #messages {
      min-height: 420px;
      max-height: 60vh;
      overflow-y: auto;
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .message {
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      padding: 14px 16px;
      border-radius: 12px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .user {
      background: #e5efff;
      margin-left: 15%;
    }

    .assistant {
      background: #f0f2f5;
      margin-right: 10%;
    }

    .sources {
      margin-top: 12px;
      font-size: 12px;
      color: #526174;
    }

    .input-area {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 18px;
      border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    }

    input {
      flex: 1;
      min-width: 0;
      padding: 14px;
      border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
      border-radius: 8px;
      font-size: 15px;
    }

    button {
      padding: 0 24px;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: #1769e0;
      color: white;
      font-size: 15px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    button:disabled {
      opacity: 0.6;
      cursor: wait;
    }

    .hint {
      text-align: center;
      color: #718096;
      font-size: 13px;
      margin: 16px;
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .input-area {
        padding: 12px;
      }

      button {
        padding: 0 16px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <header>
    <h1>Bedrock RAG Assistant</h1>
    <p>Day 2 – Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Base Demo</p>
  </header>

  <main class="container">

    <section class="chat-box">

      <div id="messages">
        <div class="message assistant">
          Hello! I am your AI knowledge assistant.
          Ask me a question about the documents in my knowledge base.
        </div>
      </div>

      <form class="input-area" id="chatForm">
        <input
          id="question"
          type="text"
          placeholder="Ask a question..."
          autocomplete="off"
          required
        >
        <button id="sendButton" type="submit">Send</button>
      </form>

    </section>

    <p class="hint">
      Powered by Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Bases and Nova Lite
    </p>

  </main>

  <script>
    const API_URL = "REPLACE_WITH_API_ENDPOINT";

    const messages = document.getElementById("messages");
    const form = document.getElementById("chatForm");
    const questionInput = document.getElementById("question");
    const sendButton = document.getElementById("sendButton");

    function addMessage(text, type, sources = []) {
      const message = document.createElement("div");
      message.className = `message ${type}`;

      const content = document.createElement("div");
      content.textContent = text;
      message.appendChild(content);

      if (sources.length > 0) {
        const sourceBox = document.createElement("div");
        sourceBox.className = "sources";

        const sourceNames = [
          ...new Set(
            sources.map(source => source.source).filter(Boolean)
          )
        ];

        sourceBox.textContent =
          "Sources: " + sourceNames.join(", ");

        message.appendChild(sourceBox);
      }

      messages.appendChild(message);
      messages.scrollTop = messages.scrollHeight;
    }

    form.addEventListener("submit", async (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();

      const question = questionInput.value.trim();

      if (!question) return;

      addMessage(question, "user");

      questionInput.value = "";
      sendButton.disabled = true;
      sendButton.textContent = "Thinking...";

      try {
        const result = await fetch(API_URL, {
          method: "POST",
          headers: {
            "Content-Type": "application/json"
          },
          body: JSON.stringify({ question })
        });

        const data = await result.json().catch(() => ({}));

        if (!result.ok) {
          throw new Error(
            data.error || `API request failed with status ${result.status}`
          );
        }

        if (!data.answer) {
          throw new Error("The API response did not contain an answer.");
        }

        addMessage(
          data.answer,
          "assistant",
          data.sources || []
        );

      } catch (error) {

        console.error("Chatbot request failed:", error);

        addMessage(
          `Error: ${error.message}`,
          "assistant"
        );

      } finally {

        sendButton.disabled = false;
        sendButton.textContent = "Send";
        questionInput.focus();

      }
    });
  </script>

</body>
</html>
EOF

